\\infty ),$ it is also continuous on $[2,\\infty ).$\n\nNotice that\n\n- $f(x)$ and $q(x)$ are not right-continuous at $x=2.$\n\n- $g(x)$ and $h(x)$ are not continuous at $x=3,$ and so are not continuous on $[2,\\infty ).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-105402/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bbfddefc-d68b-5b1e-9ec5-fd18be204d92"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-105402"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-105413/selection/3693185181b93e2d67ffc70ec92f0fa292082f7d1292a4fd90cb1470d4ac6d17" :answer/id #uuid "9d90d996-5c5f-56b3-b4e5-ba3b0f3df9f7" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13945275/assets/7afb04e0197b44ffadeee53bc365910f7c578eb8a3f2e2971a83f4f51947a3af.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105413/selection/dbc35f09cacc75cbef586ddc6e74f7d853187c1b58cf11a2a10a3c5361533df0" :answer/id #uuid "ba0de68d-ee83-5dbb-902e-926a8fbb3a98" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13945275/assets/99e22a7485ab6e5b2a086418678d90160644814965aac3a3d1aede04e7cc6f2c.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105413/selection/d9118d8db4d62b0ffc2a4714e6d6d81ee036f42013607d3c0077b5053f198746" :answer/id #uuid "37289a07-5ea1-5d3c-8214-4e125cffa24b" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13945275/assets/95587cfce50fd6e9c448bf3485dd98f7dd5bb401778b7a9fac939d356a112677.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105413/selection/823325e122286720760100c3982f83b16c85eacc990a48cc9a84c3fa5cc167ee" :answer/id #uuid "5495dd0c-bfc0-5f7a-b998-f4c459a9a3f6" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13945275/assets/24551c0a0d905070625c0d1ef76fa942dab6764